<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Jefferson returns four weeks after starting propranolol 80 mg each evening. He felt a little tired in the first week, and that has passed; he has had no dizziness, wheeze or breathlessness on his walks. His diary shows 4 migraine days in the past four weeks, each treated with sumatriptan and naproxen; he was pain-free within two hours in three of the four attacks and back at work by midday. He used no other acute medicine, so his acute-medicine days total 4. The cold he had ten days ago has gone. His diary is missing three days during the cold. He has not yet seen the occupational therapist because of a waiting list, and writing remains slow; he has started using dictation for long reports. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Propranolol</td><td>80 mg each evening for four weeks; tiredness in the first week only</td></tr><tr><td>Migraine days</td><td>4 in the past four weeks, from 13 before prevention</td></tr><tr><td>Acute medicine</td><td>Sumatriptan with naproxen on 4 days; pain-free at two hours in 3 of 4</td></tr><tr><td>Cold</td><td>Resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Occupational therapy</td><td>Not yet seen; waiting list</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

